        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2000",
        "question_text": "<p>According to Boyle's Law, the pressure of a given mass of gas is inversely proportional to its volume at constant temperature. Which of the following equations represents Boyle's Law?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Boyle's Law states that the pressure ($P$) of a given mass of gas is inversely proportional to its volume ($V$) at constant temperature. This relationship is mathematically expressed as $P \\propto \\frac{1}{V}$ or $PV = k$, where $k$ is a constant.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "22593",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "$P \\propto V$",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "96097",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "$PV = k$",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "33940",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "$V \\propto T$",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "63904",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "$P \\propto T$",
                "is_correct": false
